13	 * duplicate but still shares an existing owner's {@code lastName} (case-insensitive) and
14	 * {@code postcode} while carrying a <em>different</em> telephone. In that case the owner is
15	 * still created, but {@code possibleDuplicate} is set true and {@code possibleDuplicateOf} is
16	 * set to the matching owner's id (the lowest-id match when several exist). Otherwise
17	 * {@code possibleDuplicate} is false and {@code possibleDuplicateOf} is left absent.
18	 *
19	 * <p>A declared household member ({@code sharesHousehold} true) is never flagged: it reached this
20	 * step only because it deliberately bypassed the duplicate block, so sharing an existing owner's
21	 * last name and postcode is expected rather than a suspected duplicate.
22	 *
23	 * <p>Runs after the telephone and postcode have been normalized/assigned and before
24	 * {@link SaveOwner}, so the flags are fixed at creation time and returned on later reads.
25	 */
